-- sunholo/celestial/stellar_ld — quadratic limb-darkening coefficients, Johnson V,
-- least-squares fits, I(mu)/I(1) = 1 - a (1 - mu) - b (1 - mu)^2, from Claret & Bloemen 2011,
-- A&A 529, A75 (CDS J/A+A/529/A75, tableab.dat, sha256
-- e68d1d67e987954a0cd9f3571cda3c32e229a8fd05e61d51d3c82050af105732, fetched 2026-10-20):
--   ATLAS rows: log[M/H] = 0, microturbulence 2 km/s, every (log g, Teff) in the file
--     (Teff 3,500-50,000 K; log g 0-5 where the grid has a model);
--   PHOENIX rows: log[M/H] = 0, microturbulence 2 km/s, Teff 2,000-3,400 K, log g 3.5-5.0
--     (the cool dwarfs ATLAS does not reach: TRAPPIST-1, Barnard's Star).
-- Extracted with (shell glue, recorded so it can be redone):
--   awk 'substr($0,40,2)=="V " && substr($0,43,1)=="L"' tableab.dat > V_L.dat
--   awk 'substr($0,45,5)=="ATLAS" && substr($0,14,4)+0==0 && substr($0,19,4)+0==2' V_L.dat
--   awk 'substr($0,45,7)~/PHOENIX/ && $2<3500' V_L.dat
-- 476 ATLAS + 32 PHOENIX = 508 rows, sorted by Teff then log g (sort -k2,2n -k1,1n), each printed
--   as a record literal { logg: %.2f, teff: %.1f, a: %.4f, b: %.4f, model: 0 ATLAS | 1 PHOENIX }
--   by awk printf.

module sunholo/celestial/stellar_ld

